      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, I didn\u0027t think of this possibility. I think it\u0027s rather unlikely that reverts are created by bots, but we can\u0027t be sure about this. I checked the configs that we have at Google and actually there are more projects than I was expecting that use change.workInProgressByDefault\u003dtrue (~40, including some All-Projects project). So I wouldn\u0027t take this risk without having anyone asking for supporting change.workInProgressByDefault\u003dtrue. The current user request is just about the user preference, and I think here it\u0027s unlikely that this is set for a bot. With the new patch set I changed the change to be only about respecting the user preference. Does this resolve your concern?",
